From 207d282f3abbbe8e83ec5aa239334f109120aaa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ut-bitra <ut-bitra@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:22:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] fanotify: declare old_memcg in fanotify_alloc_event()

Commit 28293c0845cb ("BACKPORT: mm, memcg: rework remote charging API to
support nesting") converted fanotify_alloc_event() to the nesting
set_active_memcg() API but did not declare the local that holds the
previous memcg, so the file fails to build with CONFIG_FANOTIFY=y:

  fs/notify/fanotify/fanotify.c:163: error: use of undeclared identifier old_memcg

inotify_fsnotify.c received the matching declaration in the same commit.
---
 fs/notify/fanotify/fanotify.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/fs/notify/fanotify/fanotify.c b/fs/notify/fanotify/fanotify.c
index 139e5a363e3d..4e1a827eb852 100644
--- a/fs/notify/fanotify/fanotify.c
+++ b/fs/notify/fanotify/fanotify.c
@@ -147,6 +147,7 @@ struct fanotify_event_info *fanotify_alloc_event(struct fsnotify_group *group,
 {
 	struct fanotify_event_info *event = NULL;
 	gfp_t gfp = GFP_KERNEL_ACCOUNT;
+	struct mem_cgroup *old_memcg;
 
 	/*
 	 * For queues with unlimited length lost events are not expected and
